[{"id":4421302631,"node_id":"PRR_kwDONpzSS88AAAABB4e5Zw","user":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]","id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-pull-request-reviewer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Pull request overview\n\nFixes a toolchain compile failure when a single structured rule contains a `do:` sequence with multiple modifiers that apply to the same function: previously, generated trampolines / hook-context types could collide due to identical name suffixes derived from `InstFuncRule.String()`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Stamp a zero-based `do_index` onto each flat rule map produced by `rule.Normalize` for `do` sequence entries after the first.\n- Add `DoIndex` to `InstFuncRule` and incorporate it into `InstFuncRule.String()` (index 0 preserves historical naming).\n- Add regression coverage via unit tests and a new golden fixture exercising multiple hooks on one function.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 10 out of 10 changed files in this pull request and generated 1 comment.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tool/internal/setup/match_test.go | Updates normalization expectations to include `do_index` on subsequent `do` entries. |\r\n| tool/internal/rule/normalize.go | Stamps `do_index` for `do`-sequence expansions (idx > 0). |\r\n| tool/internal/rule/normalize_test.go | Updates normalization golden expectations to include `do_index`. |\r\n| tool/internal/rule/func_rule.go | Adds `DoIndex` and updates `String()` to incorporate it for unique name derivation. |\r\n| tool/internal/rule/func_rule_test.go | Adds tests pinning `String()` behavior and verifying `Normalize` stamps indices. |\r\n| tool/internal/instrument/testdata/golden/multiple-hooks-single-func/source.go | New golden fixture source for multi-hook single function case. |\r\n| tool/internal/instrument/testdata/golden/multiple-hooks-single-func/rules.yml | New structured rule with two `do` modifiers targeting the same func. |\r\n| tool/internal/instrument/testdata/golden/multiple-hooks-single-func/multi_hook.otelc.globals.go.golden | New golden globals output for the fixture. |\r\n| tool/internal/instrument/testdata/golden/multiple-hooks-single-func/multi_hook.main.go.golden | New golden instrumented output demonstrating distinct trampoline sets. |\r\n| tool/internal/instrument/testdata/golden/multiple-hooks-single-func/hook.go | New hook implementations used by the golden fixture. |\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/560#pullrequestreview-4421302631","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/560","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/560#pullrequestreview-4421302631"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/560"}},"submitted_at":"2026-06-03T17:55:32Z","commit_id":"519a4d4765934839514fa7e93daaca099885b462"},{"id":4437299558,"node_id":"PRR_kwDONpzSS88AAAABCHvRZg","user":{"login":"amazingakai","id":93782497,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZcB4Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93782497?u=636eb3c0c0e15f40e91bd088e19b41718b12ddeb&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai","html_url":"https://github.com/amazingakai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Not a blocking comment, but I wonder if we could derive the trampoline/hookcontext identifier from the rule content itself instead of an index.\n\nThe index approach can still collide in cases like:\n```yaml\nmy_hook:\n  target: main\n  where:\n    func: Func1\n  do:\n    - inject_hooks:\n        before: H1Before\n        path: \"github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pkg/instrumentation/myinst\"\n    - inject_hooks:\n        after: H1After\n        path: github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pkg/instrumentation/myinst\n\nmy_hook_1:\n  name: \"my_hook#1\"\n  target: main\n  where:\n    func: Func1\n  do:\n    - inject_hooks:\n        before: H2Before\n        path: github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pkg/instrumentation/myinst\n```\n\nIn this example, the second `do` entry of `my_hook` and the first `do` entry of `my_hook_1` would both end up producing `my_hook#1`. Admittedly this is a pretty contrived example and most users probably won't write rules like this, but the collision is still possible.\n\nInstead, we could compute a CRC32 from the flat rule content in NewInstFuncRule() and use that when generating trampoline/hookcontext names. That would make the identifiers stable regardless of ordering and avoid collisions caused by generated indices. The only remaining collision case would be when two rules have identical contents, which seems reasonable since they are effectively the same rule. WDYT?\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/560#pullrequestreview-4437299558","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/560","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/560#pullrequestreview-4437299558"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/560"}},"submitted_at":"2026-06-05T15:00:27Z","commit_id":"ae445bf14468a5b496b657933d56c51ffde73e0a"},{"id":4439776126,"node_id":"PRR_kwDONpzSS88AAAABCKGbfg","user":{"login":"txabman42","id":39015378,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDE1Mzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39015378?u=2c6cef4ddc8b8a97249b1a44ca72dfc762303ce3&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/txabman42","html_url":"https://github.com/txabman42","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/txabman42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/txabman42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/txabman42/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/txabman42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/txabman42/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/txabman42/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/txabman42/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/txabman42/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/txabman42/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think @amazingakai idea should be blocking; I'm aligned with it.\r\n\r\nRule name should be based on what it does, not on the position.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/560#pullrequestreview-4439776126","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/560","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/560#pullrequestreview-4439776126"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/560"}},"submitted_at":"2026-06-05T21:19:45Z","commit_id":"ae445bf14468a5b496b657933d56c51ffde73e0a"},{"id":4477727719,"node_id":"PRR_kwDONpzSS88AAAABCuSz5w","user":{"login":"copilot